WEBVTT

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:32.663
Let's start with the backbone
of the problem, literally.

00:01:32.704 --> 00:01:34.704
Your spine is a long structure

00:01:34.746 --> 00:01:37.579
made of bones and the cartilage discs
that sit between them.

00:01:37.621 --> 00:01:40.454
Joints, muscles and ligaments
that are attached to the bones

00:01:40.496 --> 00:01:42.663
hold it all together.

00:01:43.329 --> 00:01:47.121
A common way of sitting is with
a curved back and slumped shoulders,

00:01:47.163 --> 00:01:51.413
a position that puts uneven
pressure on your spine.

00:01:51.746 --> 00:01:55.288
Over time, this causes wear and tear
in your spinal discs,

00:01:55.329 --> 00:01:57.829
overworks certain ligaments and joints,

00:01:57.871 --> 00:02:00.204
and puts strain on muscles